  "how_to_read": {
    "speaker": "the player character whose secret backstory this is: the upload's speaker",
    "knowers": "who knows the row before anything public names it. With no knowers field: the speaker, and every person or creature on the row (a pair's two ends, an event's who), since what happens between two is known to both (#4523 ruling C). Otherwise a list of names (the only knowers), \"party\" (all four player characters), \"everyone\" (common knowledge) or \"dm\" (nobody: a real secret, not even the speaker). A node with no knowers is known to the speaker and to itself if it is a person",
    "tier": "stated = the words are in the text; inferred = only implied (offered to the DM as a suggestion, never extracted as a fact)",
    "must_find": "false = a good find if present, not a miss if absent",
    "current": "false = history: it was true and is not now",
    "line": "the line of the document's plain-text export that supports it (blank lines count)",
    "reveals": "lore_key.json's reveals lists, by id, the rows of this key the public lore states; judged by what the lore says, row by row, never by matching ends alone",
